  "prompt": "/deep-research Using https://results.aec.gov.au/, of the parties that received more than 100000 votes in the national count of the 2004 federal election in Australia for the House of Representatives, which of these parties also received more than 15000 votes in Western Australia for that election and more than 10000 votes in Queensland for that election, and more than 1% of the vote in South Australia? List these parties by their full official names, in descending order of first preference votes received in that election nationally.",
  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "Using https://results.aec.gov.au/, of the parties that received more than 100000 votes in the national count of the 2004 federal election in Australia for the House of Representatives, which of these parties also received more than 15000 votes in Western Australia for that election and more than 10000 votes in Queensland for that election, and more than 1% of the vote in South Australia? List these parties by their full official names, in descending order of first preference votes received in that election nationally.",
  "answer": "Now I have all the data. Let me analyze and apply the filters to each party.\n\n## Analysis Summary\n\n**Criteria:**\n- National first preference votes > 100,000\n- WA first preference votes > 15,000\n- QLD first preference votes > 10,000\n- SA first preference vote percentage > 1%\n\n| Party | National Votes | WA Votes | QLD Votes | SA % | Qualifies? |\n|-------|---------------|----------|-----------|------|------------|\n| Liberal | 4,741,458 | 528,016 | 867,289 | 47.40% | ✓ |\n| Australian Labor Party | 4,409,117 | 381,200 | 765,507 | 36.75% | ✓ |\n| The Greens | 841,734 | 84,100 | 111,314 | 5.44% | ✓ |\n| Democrats | 144,832 | 16,298 | 30,255 | 1.88% | ✓ |\n| One Nation | 139,956 | 27,650 | 43,619 | 1.13% | ✓ |\n| Independent | 286,206 | 14,861 | 69,589 | 2.04% | ✗ (WA < 15,000) |\n| Family First | 235,315 | 2,619 | 80,820 | 4.31% | ✗ (WA < 15,000) |\n| The Nationals | 690,275 | 6,895 | 214,522 | 1.02% | ✗ (WA < 15,000) |\n\n**Five parties meet all criteria.** Sorted by national first preference votes (descending):\n\n1. **Liberal** — 4,741,458 national votes\n2. **Australian Labor Party** — 4,409,117 national votes\n3. **The Greens** — 841,734 national votes\n4. **Democrats** — 144,832 national votes\n5. **One Nation** — 139,956 national votes\n\n---\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] National first preferences by party: https://results.aec.gov.au/12246/results/HouseStateFirstPrefsByParty-12246-NAT.htm  \n[2] WA first preferences by party: https://results.aec.gov.au/12246/results/Downloads/HouseFirstPrefsByStateByPartyDownload-12246.csv  \n[3] QLD first preferences by party: https://results.aec.gov.au/12246/results/HouseStateFirstPrefsByParty-12246-QLD.htm  \n[4] SA first preferences by party: http://results.aec.gov.au/12246/results/HouseStateFirstPrefsByParty-12246-SA.htm",
